/S /H3
/P 102 0 R
/T (Additions for n readings, window w = 7: naive: each of the \(n-6\) windows needs 6 additions, total 6\(n-6\) \(plus n-6 divisions\) = O\(7n\). Running sum: 6 for the first window, then 1 addition + 1 subtraction per later window, total 6 + 2\(n-7\) = O\(n\). For n = 365,000 that is 2,189,964 vs 729,992, a 3.0x reduction; measured time was 0.174 s vs 0.052 s \(3.3x\), matching the derived ratio.)
/E (Additions for n readings, window w = 7: naive: each of the \(n-6\) windows needs 6 additions, total 6\(n-6\) \(plus n-6 divisions\) = O\(7n\). Running sum: 6 for the first window, then 1 addition + 1 subtraction per later window, total 6 + 2\(n-7\) = O\(n\). For n = 365,000 that is 2,189,964 vs 729,992, a 3.0x reduction; measured time was 0.174 s vs 0.052 s \(3.3x\), matching the derived ratio.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [16]
>>
