/T (Time: access O\(1\) average in both designs \(list: two index operations; dict: hash of the tuple key, O\(1\) average, O\(n\) worst case on collisions\). Space: list of lists O\(rows x cols\) - the 1000 x 1000 grid used about 8.06 MB; dictionary O\(k\) for k non-empty zones - 1,000 busy zones took about 37 KB for the dict structure. The dict is far better for sparse grids, but each entry costs more \(hash table + tuple keys\), so a dense grid is smaller and faster as a list of lists.)
/E (Time: access O\(1\) average in both designs \(list: two index operations; dict: hash of the tuple key, O\(1\) average, O\(n\) worst case on collisions\). Space: list of lists O\(rows x cols\) - the 1000 x 1000 grid used about 8.06 MB; dictionary O\(k\) for k non-empty zones - 1,000 busy zones took about 37 KB for the dict structure. The dict is far better for sparse grids, but each entry costs more \(hash table + tuple keys\), so a dense grid is smaller and faster as a list of lists.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
