/Title (ravi@x.com with ravi kumar, so these 3 become 1; 'Meena' and the unnamed record share 8000000001, so 2 become 1; the two 'Anita' records have different numbers and stay separate; 'NoPhone' stays alone. Expected 3 + 2 -> 2 groups, plus 2 Anitas, plus NoPhone = 5 merged contacts, and the program printed 5. Tests covered: duplicates with different formats, a missing name, a record with no phone and no e-mail, identical names for different people, empty and None values in normalisation.)
