/Title (deque\(maxlen=7\): append\(x\) automatically discards the oldest value in O\(1\); keep a running sum, so the whole job is O\(n\) time with only O\(7\) = O\(1\) extra window space \(no new list is built per window as slicing does\). Measured 0.078 s, between naive \(0.174 s\) and the list running sum \(0.052 s\) because of Python-level deque handling.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1629 0 R
/Next 1809 0 R
>>
endobj
1744 0 obj
<<
/Title (Summary: slicing a list = O\(7n\) time, O\(n\) data + O\(7\) temporary slice; running sum = O\(n\) time, O\(1\) extra; deque = O\(n\) time, O\(1\) extra; dict = O\(n\) time, higher O\(n\) space but O\(1\) inserts.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1629 0 R
/Prev 1809 0 R
>>
