/Title (list.count\(\) version: {w: words.count\(w\) for w in set\(words\)}. Time O\(n x d\), space O\(n\) for the word list + O\(d\) for the result. Counter version: Counter\(words\) - same idea as the dictionary loop, O\(n\) time, O\(d\) space beyond the input; the counting loop runs in C so it is a little faster and shorter than a hand-written loop. The measured growth \(3.4 s at d = 5,000 vs 0.006 s\) confirms O\(n x d\) against O\(n\).)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1902 0 R
>>
