/Title (Nested loops: for each student of A scan B: O\(n xm\) time, O\(1\) extra space \(besides the result\). Sort and walk: sort both lists \(O\(n log n + m log m\)\) then advance two pointers in O\(n + m\): total O\(n log n + m log m\), O\(n + m\) space if sorted copies are made. Sets: building set\(A\) and set\(B\) is O\(n + m\) average and the intersection loops over the smaller set: O\(n + m\) average, O\(n + m\) extra space for the hash tables. Measurements agree: at 4,000 students 0.254 s \(nested\), 0.0026 s \(sorted walk\), 0.0006 s \(sets\).)
/Dest [22 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1903 0 R
>>
